<header class="site-header">
  <a class="brand" href="{{ '/' | url }}">
    {% if site.logo_url %}<img src="{{ site.logo_url }}" alt="{{ site.name }}">{% else %}{{ site.name }}{% endif %}
  </a>
  <nav aria-label="Main">
    <ul>
      {% for item in site.nav %}
        <li><a href="{{ item.href | url }}">{{ item.label }}</a></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </nav>

  {% comment %}
    The site's categories, when it keeps any: a second row under the main
    navigation, so every term's archive is one click from anywhere. The vocabulary
    name groups its terms, and it is shown even for a site with one vocabulary,
    because the name is what tells a reader what kind of thing the terms are.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% if site.taxonomy %}
    <nav class="category-nav" aria-label="Categories">
      <ul>
        {% for group in site.taxonomy %}
          <li class="category-group">
            <span class="category-group-name">{{ group.name }}</span>
            <ul>
              {% for term in group.terms %}
                <li><a href="{{ term.url | url }}">{{ term.name }}</a></li>
              {% endfor %}
            </ul>
          </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </nav>
  {% endif %}
</header>
